{"title":"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a certain school, each class has an equal number of students. If the number of classes was to increase by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then each class would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students. If the number of classes was to decrease by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then each class would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students. How many students are in each class?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the number of total students by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and number of classes by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Thus, our problem implies that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e6049d1834487b9bc02f5f0c68ad29c4df391760.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{s}{c+1} = 20 \\Longrightarrow s = 20c + 20\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"34\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c833a5cd563c72c14d2e973828c397ea4aeab4be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{s}{c-1} = 30 \\Longrightarrow s = 30c - 30\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>We solve this system of linear equations to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/b/4fb45ac08f0a40da167c4e3ade6cb5639057bcc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 5$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/d/26d93f5215a1fbb0401e9b621e14f0cba0203a23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/9/309a83b09d3c47536cb67da2834315b48d4c63c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{s}{c} = \\boxed{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>~Bradygho\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have the number of classes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/d/ebdb30c73057e8516298756a1dcd023ba6b2b75c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20(x+1)=30(x-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/c/51c80ea5862b45877f08d698a0c893bd2806a2fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Plugging back the total number of students is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7a36818c0b57d987a1801c8e550239e79304b80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{120}{5} = \\boxed{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/f/68f40b1e5cfdb4e4b37d0f5d1c57a5c893020e39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\linebreak$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"22\" />\n~Geometry285\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ol><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems\">Other 2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Answer Key\">2021 JMPSC Accuracy Answer Key</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JMPSC_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"JMPSC Problems and Solutions\">All JMPSC Problems and Solutions</a></li></ol>\n<p>The problems on this page are copyrighted by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://jmpsc.org\">Junior Mathematicians' Problem Solving Competition</a>. <span class=\"mw-valign-middle\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:JMPSC.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/120px-JMPSC.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/180px-JMPSC.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/ab/JMPSC.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018015815\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.021 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 99/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 183/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\